@startuml 05-seq-capability-resolution
' ============================================================
'  Capability tiers in action.
'  Tier 0 renders before any capability is even queried.
' ============================================================

title Capability Resolution — App Launch & Permission Lifecycle

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

actor User
participant "App bootstrap" as Boot
participant "Dashboard" as UI
participant "CapabilityRegistry" as CapReg
participant "GoogleHealthApiSource" as GHA
participant "HealthConnectSource\n«Phase 3+»" as HC
participant "HealthKitSource\n«Phase 3+»" as HK
database "Drift / SQLite" as DB

== Launch — Tier 0 renders first, unconditionally ==

Boot -> DB : open (background isolate)
activate DB
DB --> Boot : ready
deactivate DB
Boot -> UI : render
activate UI
UI -> DB : watch sessions, streaks, habits
DB -->> UI : Tier 0 + Tier 1 data

note over Boot, UI #F0FFF0
  **Attendance, streaks and logging are on screen
  before any capability is queried or any permission
  dialog is considered.** Tier 0 depends on nothing.
end note

== Tier 2 resolved asynchronously, never blocking ==

UI -> CapReg : statusFor(metrics)  «async, non-blocking»
activate CapReg

par per registered source
  CapReg -> GHA : isAvailable()
  activate GHA
  GHA -> GHA : token present? account linked?
  GHA --> CapReg : available | unavailable(reason)
  deactivate GHA
also
  CapReg -> HC : isAvailable()
  activate HC
  HC -> HC : SDK status\n(unavailable / update required / ok)
  HC --> CapReg : status
  deactivate HC
also
  CapReg -> HK : isAvailable()
  activate HK
  HK --> CapReg : status
  deactivate HK
end

CapReg -> CapReg : build per-metric map\n{metric → available | unavailable(reason)}
CapReg --> UI : CapabilityMap
deactivate CapReg

alt metric available
  UI -> DB : watch resolved snapshots
  DB -->> UI : chart renders
else metric unavailable
  UI -> UI : render empty state **with reason**
  note right of UI #FFF0F0
    e.g. "Heart-rate zones need intraday data.
    Your current source provides daily
    summaries only."
    Never a blank chart. Never a silent zero.
  end note
end
deactivate UI

== User connects a source (their choice, any time) ==

User -> UI : Settings → Connect health source
activate UI
UI -> GHA : requestPermissions(metrics)
activate GHA
GHA -> GHA : OAuth 2.0 + PKCE\n(public client, external browser)
GHA --> UI : granted | denied | partial
deactivate GHA
UI -> CapReg : invalidate()
activate CapReg
CapReg -> CapReg : re-resolve
CapReg --> UI : updated CapabilityMap
deactivate CapReg
deactivate UI

== Permissions are revocable and auto-expire ==

group Before every read
  participant "HealthSyncCoordinator" as Coord
  Coord -> CapReg : statusFor(metric)
  activate CapReg
  CapReg -> GHA : isAvailable()
  activate GHA
  alt revoked or token invalid
    GHA --> CapReg : unavailable(reason: revoked)
    deactivate GHA
    CapReg --> Coord : unavailable
    Coord -> UI : degrade to "Reconnect" card
    note right of Coord #FFF0F0
      **Never cache "granted" as durable state.**
      Permissions are revocable at any time and are
      auto-revoked after extended non-use.
      Degrade gracefully — never throw a dialog.
    end note
  else still granted
    CapReg --> Coord : available → proceed
  end
  deactivate CapReg
end

== User configures priority (per source, or per metric) ==

User -> UI : Settings → Data sources
activate UI
UI -> DB : SELECT source_priority
DB --> UI : ranked list
User -> UI : drag to reorder  «simple view»
opt advanced view
  User -> UI : override rank for a specific metric
end
UI -> DB : UPDATE source_priority(metric, source_id, rank)
DB -->> UI : resolver re-runs, dashboard updates
deactivate UI

note over User, DB #FFFDF0
  Defaults ship sensibly ranked.
  Per-metric override is available but tucked
  behind an advanced view — the primary control
  is one drag-to-reorder source list.
end note

@enduml
